.TH S3M-DU 1 "" "s3m @VERSION@" "s3m Manual"
.SH NAME
s3m\-du \- parallel object storage usage reporter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3m\-du
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fBs3://\fIBUCKET\fR[\fB/\fIPREFIX\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Summarises object storage usage by prefix, in parallel.
Output is du-style: size, a tab, then the prefix (and the storage class with \fB\-\-by\-class\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-summarize
Only print a total for each URI argument.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-max\-depth " N"
Print prefixes at most N levels below each URI.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-total
Also print a grand total.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-human\-readable
Sizes in powers of 1024.
.TP
.B \-\-si
Sizes in powers of 1000.
.TP
.B \-\-by\-class
Break every line down by storage class.
.TP
.B \-\-versions
Include non-current versions and delete markers, which is what is actually stored and billed on versioned buckets.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-threads " N"
Worker threads, 1\-256 (default 16).
.TP
.BI \-\-shard\-depth " N"
Prefix levels expanded for parallelism, 0\-9 (default 2).
.TP
.B \-\-rrdns
Resolve the endpoint hostname to every A/AAAA address and spread worker threads across them, moving a thread to the next address if its current one fails.
See
.BR s3m (7).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Write the report to FILE and show live progress.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the report on stdout; the summary is still shown.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
The connection options \fB\-\-endpoint\fR, \fB\-\-region\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR, \fB\-\-path\-style\fR, \fB\-\-no\-sign\fR, \fB\-\-insecure\fR and \fB\-\-ca\-bundle\fR are common to all s3m tools and are described in
.BR s3m (7).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success; 1 completed with errors; 2 usage, startup or safety-guard refusal.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3m (7)
.BR s3m\-ls (1)
